# Rate limiting at runtime (ADR 0006). Every order request counts per client IP and per caller
# in fixed one-minute windows; over a limit the API answers 429 with Retry-After. Every counted
# response carries RateLimit-Limit, RateLimit-Remaining and RateLimit-Reset.
#
# 1. In a terminal: `make limits PRESET=tiny` (a USER is refused after 3 requests a minute;
#    in force within 2 s locally, no deploy).
# 2. Send the four requests below within the same minute. Requests alice already made this
#    minute count too, so the 429 may come sooner.
# 3. Afterwards: `make limits PRESET=defaults` (60 a minute per USER, 300 for staff and per IP).
#
# Environment and token refresh: see orders.http (`make http-env`).

### 1 of 4: 200, RateLimit-Remaining 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 2 of 4: 200, RateLimit-Remaining 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 3 of 4: 200, RateLimit-Remaining 0
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 4 of 4: 429 rate-limited, scope "user", Retry-After = seconds to the next minute
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### Staff have their own tier: the manager is still served (tiny gives ORDER_MANAGER 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Health is never limited by the API
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health
